sDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6122a3f2.gif","alt":"The figure shows prevalence estimates of behaviors and conditions, by weighting method and telephone sample for the United States in 2010, based on Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS) data. Data are inclusive of all states and territories in BRFSS, except Tennessee and South Dakota, which lacked sufficient numbers of cellular telephone interviews in 2010. Adoption of the new methods also will result in BRFSS state-level prevalence estimates for 2011 and subsequent years that will vary from estimates that would have been achieved with previous weighting procedures. These discon¬tinuities will vary by survey question and state, and they will be driven by state-to-state variations in demographic variables used for raking and the proportion of respondents who use cellular telephones.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":630,"renderedHeight":301,"naturalWidth":630,"naturalHeight":301,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 805 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":25903},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6122a3f3.gif","alt":"The figure shows weighted prevalence estimates for current smokers, by year, weighting method, and telephone source for the United States during 2000-2010, based on Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS) data. Data are inclusive of all states and territories in BRFSS, except Tennessee and South Dakota, which lacked sufficient numbers of cellular telephone interviews in 2010. Preliminary analysis by CDC using developmental datasets for 2007-2010 reveals that, as an example, adoption of raking shifts the aggregated trend line for current smoking upward by approximately 2.3-2.8 percent¬age points for the years 2007-2010, but the shape and slope of the trend line does not change materially. The addition of cellular telephone households to the aggregated state samples for 2009 and 2010 shifts the absolute estimates slightly further upward.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":505,"renderedHeight":418,"naturalWidth":505,"naturalHeight":418,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 858 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":14808},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Microsoft Word file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1087},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_excel.gif","alt":"Microsoft Excel file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":644},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_ppt.gif","alt":"Microsoft PowerPoint file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":f